1 =

   Assigns an expression's value, an integer or a string, to a symbol.

   Format

     symbol-name =[=] expression

2 Parameters

 symbol-name

   The symbol.  One "=" makes it local to the command level, and "=="
   global.  See Symbol_Assign.

 expression

   A DCL expression: integers, quoted strings, symbols, and lexical
   functions, with DCL's operators (see Symbol_Assign Expressions).

2 Examples

   1.$ COUNT = COUNT + 1

     Adds one to the local symbol COUNT.

   2.$ NAME == F$PARSE(P1,,,"NAME")

     Gives the global symbol NAME the name part of P1.
